  result-admission WAL append, child result admission, child response receipt,
  child closure, child terminal phase, parent charge pending, parent charge
  accepted, parent charge settled, parent settlement, or child cancellation.
  Restart proves
  the result/cancellation intent remains durable without model re-entry; the
  pre-terminal windows return a named stall for the in-process provider, while
  child-terminal and parent-settled windows leave the parent task completed and
  the parent Team active awaiting coordinator finalization.
  packaged Python SDK create/run/wait path: the parent Team delegates one child
  Team, the child reaches completed, the result is admitted into the parent
  task, and the parent final is accepted by the SDK runtime.

Recovery fix validated during this matrix: Team Hub retains in-flight Team
streams during terminal recovery, so `assertParentResultStored()` reuses the
already-open parent stream instead of reopening it. This fixes the JSON
`parent-settled` restart path that previously surfaced `already-open` as a
malformed completed child journal. Team-Hub tsc, the 9-file/258-test source
matrix, JSON parent-settled restart, and the full 26-case SQLite/JSON restart
matrix pass after the fix.

This is a same-candidate matrix evidence slice. It covers thirteen independent
process crash windows on both SQLite and JSON backends and their restart
outcomes. Charge-window races may retain the parent result before or after the
selected charge record depending on append scheduling; both outcomes preserve
the no-duplicate/no-model-reentry invariant. Multi-host recovery and the
complete T-03 cross-log matrix remain open.
